You *can* teleport with the Amulet, you cannot *level teleport* with it.

One other reason why I don't find Gehennom too boring; just use those
teleportation scrolls that you typically can get in abundance, then you
don't even need to dig walls (in ordinary mazes; in special levels it's
still good to have a pick-axe or occasionally use your wands of digging).

> Something like the amulet dropping from your inventory when passing
> through a portal, so they would still be useful for escaping.

That's an unnecessary[*] complication. To escape, just drop the Amulet
and escape by ordinary levelport using a cursed scroll of teleportation.
As a reason to introduce a new portal feature that is not convincing.
A cursed scroll can be applied anywhere, it's not bound to a specific
location that you have to visit and it doesn't require introducing a
new item or dungeon feature.

